#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""The scoreboard of docs/NORTH-STAR.md, rendered from the records in the tree (#77).

    tools/scoreboard                    print the table the records give
    tools/scoreboard --render           rewrite the table between the markers of docs/NORTH-STAR.md
    tools/scoreboard --check            exit 1 with a diff when the committed table is stale, or
                                        when a floor stands above its measured score (rule 1 below)
    tools/scoreboard --check --base F   also exit 1 when a number fell from the base's values F
    tools/scoreboard --json             print the tree's comparable values (the --base input)
    --root DIR                          read the tree at DIR instead of this checkout

The table lives between `<!-- scoreboard:begin -->` and `<!-- scoreboard:end -->`
and is never edited by hand: a PR that moves a record (re-records the ratchet,
adds a fixture, moves a floor) runs --render and commits the table with it; the
CI job `ratchet` runs --check against the values of the base ref's tree, which
it renders with --json (--root on the base's tree, read with git archive, as
the ratchet's own step reads the base record). A Python script with the
standard library only, like tools/ratchet. It reads files and runs no cargo,
no git and no network.

The base is rendered by the BASE'S OWN copy of this tool (git show
<base>:tools/scoreboard, run with --root on the base's tree), never by the
PR's: a PR controls its tree and its tool, so a base its tool rendered would be
a base the PR chose. Only while the base holds no tools/scoreboard is this
tree's copy used, and the step's log says which. The comparisons, ceiling() and
falls(), are the tree's, so a PR that weakens them is a diff of this file for its review to
read. That a weakened tree tool cannot change what the base's tool renders is
not testable in-process (the planted cases run one copy); this rule and the CI
step hold it.

A record that is MISSING renders as a row that says so ("not in the tree yet",
"unmeasured", "no baseline yet", "no report yet"). A record that is PRESENT must match its shape
below, or the tool exits 1 naming the file and the field; it never reads a
malformed record as an absent one.

  docs/ratchets.json             {"commit": <40-hex sha>, "ratchets": {name: int}}
  tests/wire/MANIFEST.json       {"fixtures": [names]}: the wire fixtures
  tests/wire_consumers/          the consumers' fixtures: every file is
                                 <consumer>/<name>.json, one directory per consumer
  tests/arch_*.rs                the architecture rules (#73): each file holds one
                                 `const ALLOWED: &[(&str, usize, &str)] = &[..];` of
                                 ("src/file.rs", count, "reason") tuples and one
                                 `const RULE: Rule = Rule { name: "A<n>: .." ..`; the
                                 rows count the allowlist's own data, never a doc
  .github/workflows/nightly.yml  the mutation floors: the JSON object of MUTANTS_FLOORS
  docs/scoreboard/mutants.json   the measured scores, written by the captain from the
                                 nightly's "Mutation score" summary (shape below)
  fuzz/Cargo.toml                the fuzz targets: its [[bin]] tables' names, read with
                                 tomllib, never a list written here
  docs/scoreboard/fuzz.json      the fuzz hours, written by the captain or a lane from
                                 the Nightly run it names (shape below)
  docs/scoreboard/differential.json
                                 the differential report, written by the captain or a
                                 lane from the Differential run it names (shape below)
  benches/baseline.json          the bench baseline, tools/bench-compare's shape:
                                 {"profiles": {name: {"runs": [{"benches": {id:
                                 {"p50_us": n, "p99_us": n, ..}}}]}}}
  tests/e2e/scenarios/*.js       the e2e scenarios: run.js requires every .js there and
                                 calls each module's run(walletA, walletB, assert), so
                                 a scenario is a file whose code exports a run
                                 (`module.exports = { .. run .. }` or
                                 `module.exports.run =`); another .js is not counted
  tests/e2e/run.js, lib/*.js     the hermetic flag: present when the code (comments
                                 and string literals blanked) reads the knob,
                                 `process.env.E2E_HERMETIC` or `process.env['E2E_HERMETIC']`

docs/scoreboard/mutants.json, the measured column of the floors' rows:

  {
    "schema": 1,
    "commit": "<the full sha the nightly mutated>",
    "run": "<the nightly run's URL>",
    "date": "YYYY-MM-DD",
    "files": {
      "src/spend_gate.rs": {"score": 86.6, "caught": 194, "missed": 30,
                            "timeout": 0, "unviable": 12}
    }
  }

`score` is the summary's score column (caught / (caught + missed + timeout) * 100,
.github/nightly/mutants_score.py); the counts are its columns, and the score must
equal the one they give, to one place (mutation_score(), the nightly's formula), or
the tool exits 1 naming the file, the stored score and the computed one: a score is
never read as given, since the ceiling holds a floor under it. A file whose caught,
missed and timeout are all 0 is malformed. The table shows the score and the commit. A floored file the object does
not name reads "unmeasured", as every floor does while the file is absent.

docs/scoreboard/fuzz.json, the fuzz hours' rows, one per target of fuzz/Cargo.toml:

  {
    "schema": 1,
    "commit": "<the full sha the night fuzzed>",
    "run": "https://github.com/Calhooon/bsv-wallet-cli/actions/runs/<id>",
    "date": "YYYY-MM-DD",
    "targets": {
      "beef_reader": {"seconds": 3600, "executions": 41000000,
                      "corpus_added": 12, "crashes": 0}
    }
  }

`seconds` is the target's fuzzing time in that run (a number above 0; the row's
value is it in hours, to one place, the run's own and never a sum across runs);
`executions`, `corpus_added` and `crashes` are the job's libFuzzer statistics and
its summary's corpus additions, counts. The run is a URL under
https://github.com/Calhooon/bsv-wallet-cli/actions/runs/, as the record of every
census cell is (this record and the next; mutants.json predates the rule). A
target the record names and the manifest does not is malformed; a target the
manifest names and the record does not reads "unmeasured", as every target does
while the file is absent. The measured column shows the counts and the commit; a
crash count above 0 shows with its number, never hidden.

docs/scoreboard/differential.json, the differential's row:

  {
    "schema": 1,
    "run": "https://github.com/Calhooon/bsv-wallet-cli/actions/runs/<id>",
    "date": "YYYY-MM-DD",
    "base": "<the full sha of the base build>",
    "head": "<the full sha of the head build>",
    "differences": 0, "calls": 900, "commands": 40, "complete": true,
    "same_floor": {"differences": 0, "calls": 900, "commands": 40}
  }

The figures of tools/differential's own verdict line, `DIFFERENTIAL: N differences
over C calls and M commands`, with `complete` false when the line is INCOMPLETE
(a recording that is not a whole run), and of the --same floor's line on the
head. A complete report, and the floor, ran calls and commands: either at 0 is
malformed, since tools/differential reads no calls or no commands as INCOMPLETE.
The row's value is the differences, or INCOMPLETE and never a verdict when
`complete` is false; while the file is absent it reads "no report yet".

The values --json prints and --base reads: {"schema": 1, "values": {key: value}}.
A key `floor:<file>`, `fixtures:wire`, `fixtures:consumers`, `consumers`,
`e2e:scenarios`, `e2e:hermetic` (1 or 0) or `arch:rules` is a number that may
not fall below the base's; a key `allowlist:<rule>:files` or
`allowlist:<rule>:sites` is a number that may not rise above the base's; a key
`arch:rule-ids`, `floor:files`, `consumers:names` or `fuzz:target-names` is the
sorted list of the rule ids, floored files, consumer names or measured fuzz
targets, and may not lose an element the base's holds (a count can be kept by a swap, a list cannot: renaming rule A3 to
A9, or deleting A4's file and adding an empty A7, keeps `arch:rules` and loses
an element). A key `fuzz:targets` (the count of the targets the fuzz record
measures) or `differential:complete` (1 or 0) may not fall; a key
`fuzz:<target>:crashes` or `differential:same_floor` (the floor's differences,
whose only right value is 0) may not rise. A key `fuzz:<target>:seconds` is the
latest run's seconds, which a later run of one hour replaces, so it is held to no
direction: only to not vanishing. A key the base holds may not vanish from the
tree, of any kind.
The ratchets' own numbers are tools/ratchet's to compare.

A key `floor:<file>:measured` (true or false) says whether
docs/scoreboard/mutants.json names the file. A floor is measured when the
record names its file and provisional when it does not. The floors' rule:

  1. The ceiling. A floor whose file the tree's record measures is never above
     that score rounded down, whether it rose, stayed, fell or is new. It is a
     property of the tree alone, so every --check holds it, with a base or
     without one (CI on a push whose previous commit cannot be fetched), for
     every floor of MUTANTS_FLOORS; a fault names the file, the floor and the
     score.
  2. The fall (--base). A floor with a measurement at the base never falls; a
     provisional floor never falls without a measurement in the tree's record;
     a measurement at the base never vanishes from the tree.
  3. The first measurement (--base). A provisional floor at the base whose file
     the tree's record measures may fall once, and then to exactly the measured
     score rounded down, never any lower (and, by 1, never higher); the check
     prints a notice naming the file and both floors.
  4. The provisional notice. A floor of the tree with no measurement is allowed
     as a provisional floor, held to no score, and every --check prints a notice
     naming it.

A base rendered by a tool older than the `:measured` key carries no such key,
and every floor of it reads as unmeasured: such a base also predates
docs/scoreboard/mutants.json, which landed with the key (#76). A base that
carries the key for some floors and not for another is a fault.
"""

import argparse
import difflib
import json
import math
import re
import sys
from pathlib import Path

ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
BEGIN = "<!-- scoreboard:begin -->"
END = "<!-- scoreboard:end -->"

DOC = "docs/NORTH-STAR.md"
RATCHETS = "docs/ratchets.json"
WIRE = "tests/wire/MANIFEST.json"
CONSUMERS = "tests/wire_consumers"
ARCH_GLOB = "tests/arch_*.rs"
NIGHTLY = ".github/workflows/nightly.yml"
MUTANTS = "docs/scoreboard/mutants.json"
FUZZ_MANIFEST = "fuzz/Cargo.toml"
FUZZ = "docs/scoreboard/fuzz.json"
DIFFERENTIAL = "docs/scoreboard/differential.json"
BENCH = "benches/baseline.json"
SCENARIOS = "tests/e2e/scenarios"
HERMETIC_FILES = ["tests/e2e/run.js", "tests/e2e/lib/*.js"]

ABSENT = "not in the tree yet"
SHA = re.compile(r"^[0-9a-f]{40}$")
DATE = re.compile(r"^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}$")
RUNS = "https://github.com/Calhooon/bsv-wallet-cli/actions/runs/"
RUN_URL = re.compile(r"^" + re.escape(RUNS) + r"\d+(/attempts/\d+)?$")
TARGET = re.compile(r"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$")

# A key's direction: "floor" may not fall (nor leave the tree), "ceiling" may not rise.
FLOOR_KEYS = re.compile(r"^(floor:.+|fixtures:wire|fixtures:consumers|consumers|e2e:scenarios|e2e:hermetic|arch:rules"
                        r"|fuzz:targets|differential:complete)$")
CEILING_KEYS = re.compile(r"^(allowlist:A\d+:(files|sites)|fuzz:[^:]+:crashes|differential:same_floor)$")
# A number held to no direction, only to not vanishing: the latest run's seconds.
LATEST_KEYS = re.compile(r"^fuzz:[^:]+:seconds$")
# A floor's flag: whether docs/scoreboard/mutants.json measured its file (a bool).
MEASURED_KEYS = re.compile(r"^floor:.+:measured$")
# A key whose value is a sorted list of names: it may not lose an element.
LIST_KEYS = re.compile(r"^(arch:rule-ids|floor:files|consumers:names|fuzz:target-names)$")


def path(name):
    return ROOT / name


def fail(name, field, why):
    raise SystemExit(f"scoreboard: {name}: {field}: {why}")


def is_int(v):
    return isinstance(v, int) and not isinstance(v, bool)


def is_num(v):
    """A finite number: Python's json reads Infinity, -Infinity and NaN as floats,
    and --json would print them back as no JSON at all."""
    return isinstance(v, (int, float)) and not isinstance(v, bool) and math.isfinite(v)


def load_json(name):
    """A present record's JSON; an empty or unparsable file is a fault, never an absence."""
    text = path(name).read_text()
    if not text.strip():
        fail(name, "(the file)", "present and empty; a record that is not measured yet is absent, not empty")
    try:
        return json.loads(text)
    except json.JSONDecodeError as e:
        fail(name, "(the file)", f"not JSON ({e})")


def require_object(name, field, v):
    if not isinstance(v, dict):
        fail(name, field, f"must be an object, is {type(v).__name__}")
    return v


class Row:
    def __init__(self, row, value, measured="", record="", values=None):
        self.cells = (row, value, measured, record)
        self.values = values or {}


def ratchet_rows():
    if not path(RATCHETS).exists():
        return [Row("ratchets", ABSENT, "", f"`{RATCHETS}`")]
    record = require_object(RATCHETS, "(the file)", load_json(RATCHETS))
    commit = record.get("commit")
    if not isinstance(commit, str) or not SHA.match(commit):
        fail(RATCHETS, "commit", "must be a full 40-hex sha")
    ratchets = require_object(RATCHETS, "ratchets", record.get("ratchets"))
    if not ratchets:
        fail(RATCHETS, "ratchets", "holds no ratchet")
    for key, value in ratchets.items():
        if not is_int(value) or value < 0:
            fail(RATCHETS, f"ratchets.{key}", "must be a count (an integer at least 0)")
    source = f"`{RATCHETS}` at {commit[:7]}"
    return [Row(f"ratchet `{key}`", str(value), "", source) for key, value in ratchets.items()]


def wire_rows():
    if not path(WIRE).exists():
        return [Row("wire fixtures", ABSENT, "", f"`{WIRE}`")]
    fixtures = require_object(WIRE, "(the file)", load_json(WIRE)).get("fixtures")
    if not isinstance(fixtures, list) or not all(isinstance(f, str) and f for f in fixtures):
        fail(WIRE, "fixtures", "must be a list of fixture names")
    if len(set(fixtures)) != len(fixtures):
        fail(WIRE, "fixtures", "names a fixture twice")
    return [Row("wire fixtures", str(len(fixtures)), "", f"`{WIRE}`", {"fixtures:wire": len(fixtures)})]


def consumer_rows():
    source = f"`{CONSUMERS}/`"
    base = path(CONSUMERS)
    if not base.is_dir():
        return [Row("consumers' fixtures", ABSENT, "", source)]
    fixtures = []
    for p in sorted(base.rglob("*")):
        if p.is_dir():
            continue
        parts = p.relative_to(base).parts
        if len(parts) != 2 or not parts[1].endswith(".json"):
            fail(CONSUMERS, p.relative_to(base).as_posix(),
                 "every file is <consumer>/<name>.json; this one is not")
        fixtures.append(parts)
    consumers = {c for c, _ in fixtures}
    if not fixtures:
        fail(CONSUMERS, "(the directory)", "present and holds no fixture")
    value = f"{len(fixtures)} over {len(consumers)} consumers"
    return [Row("consumers' fixtures", value, "", source,
                {"fixtures:consumers": len(fixtures), "consumers": len(consumers),
                 "consumers:names": sorted(consumers)})]


# One tuple of an allowlist: ("src/file.rs", 12, "the reason"), a trailing comma allowed.
# A string is a Rust string literal, read by rust_str(), never as JSON: the two
# escape sets differ (\' and \u{..} and a line continuation are Rust's alone).
STR = r'"(?:[^"\\]|\\.)*"'
# A raw string, r"..", r#".."#, opening either string of a tuple: refused by name.
RAW = re.compile(r'\(\s*(?:"(?:[^"\\]|\\.)*"\s*,\s*\d+\s*,\s*)?r#*"', re.S)
SIMPLE_ESCAPES = {"n": "\n", "r": "\r", "t": "\t", "\\": "\\", "0": "\0", "'": "'", '"': '"'}
HEX = set("0123456789abcdefABCDEF")
TUPLE = re.compile(r'\(\s*(' + STR + r')\s*,\s*(\d+)\s*,\s*(' + STR + r')\s*,?\s*\)\s*(?:,|$)\s*', re.S)
ALLOWED_OPEN = "const ALLOWED: &[(&str, usize, &str)] = &["
RULE_NAME = re.compile(r'const RULE: Rule = Rule \{\s*name:\s*"(A\d+): [^"]+",')


def rust_str(lit, name, field):
    """The value of a Rust string literal `"..."` (STR's match), as rustc reads it:
    \\n \\r \\t \\\\ \\0 \\' \\", \\x00 to \\x7f, \\u{1 to 6 hex digits} (a scalar value),
    and a backslash before a newline, which drops the newline and the whitespace
    after it. Any other escape is a fault, never a traceback."""
    body, out, i = lit[1:-1], [], 0
    while i < len(body):
        c = body[i]
        if c != "\\":
            out.append(c)
            i += 1
            continue
        e = body[i + 1] if i + 1 < len(body) else ""
        if e in SIMPLE_ESCAPES:
            out.append(SIMPLE_ESCAPES[e])
            i += 2
        elif e in ("\n", "\r"):
            if e == "\r" and body[i + 2:i + 3] != "\n":
                fail(name, field, "a bare carriage return after a backslash is not a Rust escape")
            i += 2
            while i < len(body) and body[i] in " \t\n\r":
                i += 1
        elif e == "x":
            digits = body[i + 2:i + 4]
            if len(digits) != 2 or not set(digits) <= HEX or int(digits, 16) > 0x7F:
                fail(name, field, f"\\x{digits} is not a Rust escape (two hex digits, at most 7f)")
            out.append(chr(int(digits, 16)))
            i += 4
        elif e == "u":
            close = body.find("}", i + 3)
            if body[i + 2:i + 3] != "{" or close < 0:
                fail(name, field, "\\u without braces is not a Rust escape (\\u{1 to 6 hex digits})")
            digits = body[i + 3:close]
            v = digits.replace("_", "")
            if (digits.startswith("_") or not 1 <= len(v) <= 6 or not set(v) <= HEX
                    or int(v, 16) > 0x10FFFF or 0xD800 <= int(v, 16) <= 0xDFFF):
                fail(name, field, f"{body[i:close + 1]} is not a Rust escape (\\u{{1 to 6 hex digits}}, a scalar value)")
            out.append(chr(int(v, 16)))
            i = close + 1
        else:
            fail(name, field, f"\\{e} is not a Rust escape")
    return "".join(out)


def allowlist(name, text):
    """The (file, count) tuples of the file's one ALLOWED literal, read strictly."""
    if text.count(ALLOWED_OPEN) != 1:
        fail(name, "ALLOWED", f"must hold `{ALLOWED_OPEN}` exactly once")
    body = text.split(ALLOWED_OPEN, 1)[1]
    end = body.find("\n];")
    if end < 0:
        fail(name, "ALLOWED", "the literal does not close with `];` on its own line")
    body, pos, entries = body[:end], 0, []
    body = body.strip()
    while pos < len(body):
        entry = f"ALLOWED entry {len(entries) + 1}"
        if RAW.match(body, pos):
            fail(name, entry, 'a raw string r"..", r#".."# is not read; write it as a plain "..." literal')
        m = TUPLE.match(body, pos)
        if not m:
            snippet = body[pos:pos + 60].split("\n")[0]
            fail(name, entry, f"not a (\"file\", count, \"reason\") tuple: {snippet!r}")
        if "\\" in m.group(1):
            fail(name, entry, f"the file {m.group(1)} carries an escape; a src/ path never does")
        file, count = m.group(1)[1:-1], int(m.group(2))
        if not file.startswith("src/") or not file.endswith(".rs"):
            fail(name, entry, f"{file!r} is not a src/ .rs file")
        if count == 0:
            fail(name, entry, f"{file} counts 0; an entry at zero is removed")
        if not rust_str(m.group(3), name, f"{entry} ({file}'s reason)").strip():
            fail(name, entry, f"{file} carries no reason")
        entries.append((file, count))
        pos = m.end()
    files = [f for f, _ in entries]
    if len(set(files)) != len(files):
        fail(name, "ALLOWED", "names a file twice")
    return entries


def arch_rows():
    tests = sorted(ROOT.glob(ARCH_GLOB))
    if not tests:
        return [Row("architecture rules", ABSENT, "", f"`{ARCH_GLOB}`")]
    rules = {}
    for p in tests:
        name = p.relative_to(ROOT).as_posix()
        try:
            text = p.read_text()
        except (OSError, UnicodeDecodeError) as e:
            fail(name, "(the file)", f"not readable as UTF-8 ({e})")
        names = RULE_NAME.findall(text)
        if len(names) != 1:
            fail(name, "RULE", 'must hold one `const RULE: Rule = Rule { name: "A<n>: ..",`')
        rule = names[0]
        if rule in rules:
            fail(name, "RULE", f"{rule} is also {rules[rule][0]}'s rule")
        rules[rule] = (name, allowlist(name, text))
    ids = sorted(rules, key=lambda r: int(r[1:]))
    rows = [Row("architecture rules", str(len(rules)), "", f"`{ARCH_GLOB}`",
                {"arch:rules": len(rules), "arch:rule-ids": ids})]
    for rule in ids:
        name, entries = rules[rule]
        files, sites = len(entries), sum(c for _, c in entries)
        rows.append(Row(f"arch rule {rule} allowlist", f"{files} files, {sites} sites", "", f"`{name}` ALLOWED",
                        {f"allowlist:{rule}:files": files, f"allowlist:{rule}:sites": sites}))
    return rows


def floors():
    """MUTANTS_FLOORS from nightly.yml: the folded scalar after the key, read as JSON."""
    lines = path(NIGHTLY).read_text().splitlines()
    found = [i for i, line in enumerate(lines) if re.match(r"\s*MUTANTS_FLOORS:", line)]
    if len(found) != 1:
        fail(NIGHTLY, "MUTANTS_FLOORS", f"must be set once, is set {len(found)} times")
    i = found[0]
    m = re.match(r"(\s*)MUTANTS_FLOORS:\s*(.*)$", lines[i])
    indent, rest = len(m.group(1)), m.group(2).strip()
    if rest and rest not in (">", ">-", "|", "|-"):
        text = rest.strip("'\"")
    else:
        body = []
        for nxt in lines[i + 1:]:
            if nxt.strip() and len(nxt) - len(nxt.lstrip()) <= indent:
                break
            body.append(nxt.strip())
        text = " ".join(body)
    try:
        value = json.loads(text)
    except json.JSONDecodeError as e:
        fail(NIGHTLY, "MUTANTS_FLOORS", f"not a JSON object ({e})")
    require_object(NIGHTLY, "MUTANTS_FLOORS", value)
    if not value:
        fail(NIGHTLY, "MUTANTS_FLOORS", "holds no floor")
    for file, floor in value.items():
        if not is_num(floor) or not 0 <= floor <= 100:
            fail(NIGHTLY, f"MUTANTS_FLOORS.{file}", "must be a score from 0 to 100")
    return value


def mutation_score(caught, missed, timeout):
    """The nightly's own score (.github/nightly/mutants_score.py, its table):
    caught over the judged (a timeout weighs as a miss), to one place."""
    return round(100.0 * caught / (caught + missed + timeout), 1)


def measured_scores():
    """docs/scoreboard/mutants.json's scores, by file; {} when the record is absent."""
    if not path(MUTANTS).exists():
        return {}, ""
    record = require_object(MUTANTS, "(the file)", load_json(MUTANTS))
    if record.get("schema") != 1:
        fail(MUTANTS, "schema", "must be 1")
    commit = record.get("commit")
    if not isinstance(commit, str) or not SHA.match(commit):
        fail(MUTANTS, "commit", "must be the full 40-hex sha the nightly mutated")
    if not isinstance(record.get("run"), str) or not record["run"]:
        fail(MUTANTS, "run", "must be the nightly run's URL")
    if not isinstance(record.get("date"), str) or not DATE.match(record["date"]):
        fail(MUTANTS, "date", "must be YYYY-MM-DD")
    files = require_object(MUTANTS, "files", record.get("files"))
    if not files:
        fail(MUTANTS, "files", "holds no file; a nightly that measured nothing is not a record")
    scores = {}
    for file, entry in files.items():
        require_object(MUTANTS, f"files.{file}", entry)
        if not is_num(entry.get("score")) or not 0 <= entry["score"] <= 100:
            fail(MUTANTS, f"files.{file}.score", "must be a score from 0 to 100")
        for n in ("caught", "missed", "timeout", "unviable"):
            if not is_int(entry.get(n)) or entry[n] < 0:
                fail(MUTANTS, f"files.{file}.{n}", "must be a count (an integer at least 0)")
        judged = entry["caught"] + entry["missed"] + entry["timeout"]
        if judged == 0:
            fail(MUTANTS, f"files.{file}", "caught + missed + timeout is 0; a file no mutant judged has no score")
        computed = mutation_score(entry["caught"], entry["missed"], entry["timeout"])
        if entry["score"] != computed:
            fail(MUTANTS, f"files.{file}.score",
                 f"{entry['score']:g} stored, {computed:g} computed from its counts "
                 f"(100 * caught / (caught + missed + timeout), to one place); the score is its counts'")
        scores[file] = entry["score"]
    return scores, commit[:7]


def mutation_rows():
    if not path(NIGHTLY).exists():
        return [Row("mutation floors", ABSENT, "", f"`{NIGHTLY}`")]
    scores, commit = measured_scores()
    rows, named = [], sorted(floors().items())
    for file, floor in named:
        score = scores.get(file)
        cell = "unmeasured" if score is None else f"{score:.1f} at {commit}"
        rows.append(Row(f"mutation floor `{file}`", f"{floor:g}", cell, f"`{NIGHTLY}`",
                        {f"floor:{file}": floor, f"floor:{file}:measured": score is not None}))
    rows[0].values["floor:files"] = [file for file, _ in named]
    return rows


def require_run(name, record, what):
    run = record.get("run")
    if not isinstance(run, str) or not RUN_URL.match(run):
        fail(name, "run", f"must be the {what} run's URL, {RUNS}<id>")
    return run


def require_date(name, record):
    if not isinstance(record.get("date"), str) or not DATE.match(record["date"]):
        fail(name, "date", "must be YYYY-MM-DD")


def require_count(name, field, v):
    if not is_int(v) or v < 0:
        fail(name, field, "must be a count (an integer at least 0)")
    return v


def fuzz_targets():
    """The [[bin]] names of fuzz/Cargo.toml, in its order: the targets the Nightly runs."""
    import tomllib
    try:
        manifest = tomllib.loads(path(FUZZ_MANIFEST).read_text())
    except tomllib.TOMLDecodeError as e:
        fail(FUZZ_MANIFEST, "(the file)", f"not TOML ({e})")
    bins = manifest.get("bin")
    if not isinstance(bins, list) or not bins:
        fail(FUZZ_MANIFEST, "[[bin]]", "names no target")
    names = []
    for i, b in enumerate(bins):
        if not isinstance(b, dict) or not isinstance(b.get("name"), str) or not TARGET.match(b["name"]):
            fail(FUZZ_MANIFEST, f"[[bin]] {i + 1}", "must carry a name of letters, digits, _ and -")
        names.append(b["name"])
    if len(set(names)) != len(names):
        fail(FUZZ_MANIFEST, "[[bin]]", "names a target twice")
    return names


def fuzz_rows():
    if not path(FUZZ_MANIFEST).exists():
        if path(FUZZ).exists():
            fail(FUZZ, "(the file)", f"present, and {FUZZ_MANIFEST} is absent: no target to measure")
        return [Row("fuzz hours", ABSENT, "", f"`{FUZZ_MANIFEST}`")]
    targets, source = fuzz_targets(), f"`{FUZZ}`"
    if not path(FUZZ).exists():
        rows = [Row(f"fuzz hours `{t}`", "unmeasured", "", source) for t in targets]
        rows[0].values.update({"fuzz:targets": 0, "fuzz:target-names": []})
        return rows
    record = require_object(FUZZ, "(the file)", load_json(FUZZ))
    if record.get("schema") != 1:
        fail(FUZZ, "schema", "must be 1")
    commit = record.get("commit")
    if not isinstance(commit, str) or not SHA.match(commit):
        fail(FUZZ, "commit", "must be the full 40-hex sha the night fuzzed")
    run = require_run(FUZZ, record, "Nightly")
    require_date(FUZZ, record)
    measured = require_object(FUZZ, "targets", record.get("targets"))
    if not measured:
        fail(FUZZ, "targets", "holds no target; a night that fuzzed nothing is not a record")
    for t, entry in measured.items():
        if t not in targets:
            fail(FUZZ, f"targets.{t}", f"is not a target of {FUZZ_MANIFEST} ({', '.join(targets)})")
        require_object(FUZZ, f"targets.{t}", entry)
        if not is_num(entry.get("seconds")) or not entry["seconds"] > 0:
            fail(FUZZ, f"targets.{t}.seconds", "must be a number of seconds above 0")
        for n in ("executions", "corpus_added", "crashes"):
            require_count(FUZZ, f"targets.{t}.{n}", entry.get(n))
    rows = []
    for t in targets:
        e = measured.get(t)
        if e is None:
            rows.append(Row(f"fuzz hours `{t}`", "unmeasured", "", source))
            continue
        cell = (f"{e['executions']} executions, {e['corpus_added']} corpus, "
                f"{e['crashes']} crashes at {commit[:7]}")
        rows.append(Row(f"fuzz hours `{t}`", f"{e['seconds'] / 3600:.1f}", cell, run,
                        {f"fuzz:{t}:seconds": e["seconds"], f"fuzz:{t}:crashes": e["crashes"]}))
    names = sorted(t for t in targets if t in measured)
    rows[0].values.update({"fuzz:targets": len(names), "fuzz:target-names": names})
    return rows


def differential_rows():
    if not path(DIFFERENTIAL).exists():
        return [Row("differential", "no report yet", "", f"`{DIFFERENTIAL}`")]
    name = DIFFERENTIAL
    record = require_object(name, "(the file)", load_json(name))
    if record.get("schema") != 1:
        fail(name, "schema", "must be 1")
    run = require_run(name, record, "Differential")
    require_date(name, record)
    for side in ("base", "head"):
        if not isinstance(record.get(side), str) or not SHA.match(record[side]):
            fail(name, side, f"must be the full 40-hex sha of the {side} build")
    for n in ("differences", "calls", "commands"):
        require_count(name, n, record.get(n))
    if not isinstance(record.get("complete"), bool):
        fail(name, "complete", "must be true or false (false: the verdict line was INCOMPLETE)")
    floor = require_object(name, "same_floor", record.get("same_floor"))
    for n in ("differences", "calls", "commands"):
        require_count(name, f"same_floor.{n}", floor.get(n))
    for prefix, rec in (("", record), ("same_floor.", floor)):
        for n in ("calls", "commands"):
            if (rec is floor or record["complete"]) and rec[n] == 0:
                fail(name, f"{prefix}{n}", "0 in a whole run; a run makes calls and commands, and "
                     "tools/differential reads 0 of either as INCOMPLETE")
    complete = record["complete"]
    word = "complete" if complete else "INCOMPLETE"
    cell = (f"{record['calls']} calls, {record['commands']} commands; "
            f"the same-build floor {floor['differences']}; {word}")
    value = str(record["differences"]) if complete else "INCOMPLETE"
    return [Row(f"differential `{record['head'][:7]}` against `{record['base'][:7]}`", value, cell, run,
                {"differential:same_floor": floor["differences"], "differential:complete": 1 if complete else 0})]


def bench_rows():
    source = f"`{BENCH}`"
    if not path(BENCH).exists():
        return [Row("bench baseline", "no baseline yet", "", source)]
    record = require_object(BENCH, "(the file)", load_json(BENCH))
    profiles = require_object(BENCH, "profiles", record.get("profiles"))
    if not profiles:
        return [Row("bench baseline", "no entry yet", "", source)]
    rows = []
    for name, entry in sorted(profiles.items()):
        require_object(BENCH, f"profiles.{name}", entry)
        runs = entry.get("runs")
        if not isinstance(runs, list) or not runs:
            fail(BENCH, f"profiles.{name}.runs", "must be a list of at least one run")
        ids = None
        for i, run in enumerate(runs):
            benches = require_object(BENCH, f"profiles.{name}.runs[{i}].benches",
                                     require_object(BENCH, f"profiles.{name}.runs[{i}]", run).get("benches"))
            if not benches:
                fail(BENCH, f"profiles.{name}.runs[{i}].benches", "holds no bench")
            for id, m in benches.items():
                for n in ("p50_us", "p99_us"):
                    if not is_num(require_object(BENCH, f"profiles.{name}.runs[{i}].benches.{id}", m).get(n)):
                        fail(BENCH, f"profiles.{name}.runs[{i}].benches.{id}.{n}", "must be a number")
            if ids is not None and set(benches) != ids:
                fail(BENCH, f"profiles.{name}.runs[{i}].benches", "measures other bench ids than run 0")
            ids = set(benches)
        rows.append(Row(f"bench baseline `{name}`", f"{len(ids)} benches, {len(runs)} runs", "", source))
    return rows


IDENT = re.compile(r"^[A-Za-z_$][\w$]*$")
# A `/` after one of these (or at the start) opens a regular expression literal.
REGEX_AFTER = set("(,=:[!&|?{};+-*%<>~^")


def opens_regex(before):
    last = before.rstrip()[-1:]
    return not last or last in REGEX_AFTER


def code_text(text):
    """A JavaScript file's code: comments blanked (their newlines kept) and every
    string, template or regular expression literal blanked to '' unless its body is
    a bare identifier (kept, so `process.env['E2E_HERMETIC']` and a quoted key
    `'run':` still read as code). A mention of the knob in a comment or a string
    ("process.env.E2E_HERMETIC") is never a read."""
    out, i, n = [], 0, len(text)
    while i < n:
        c = text[i]
        if text.startswith("//", i):
            j = text.find("\n", i)
            i = n if j < 0 else j
        elif text.startswith("/*", i):
            j = text.find("*/", i + 2)
            j = n if j < 0 else j + 2
            out.append("\n" * text.count("\n", i, j))
            i = j
        elif c in "'\"`" or (c == "/" and opens_regex("".join(out))):
            j, klass = i + 1, False
            while j < n and (text[j] != c or klass) and not (c in "'\"" and text[j] == "\n"):
                if text[j] == "\\":
                    j += 1
                elif c == "/" and text[j] in "[]":
                    klass = text[j] == "["
                j += 1
            body = text[i + 1:j]
            out.append(c + (body if c != "/" and IDENT.match(body) else "") + c)
            out.append("\n" * body.count("\n"))
            i = j + 1
        else:
            out.append(c)
            i += 1
    return "".join(out)


KNOB = re.compile(r"process\.env(?:\s*\.\s*E2E_HERMETIC\b|\s*\[\s*(['\"`])E2E_HERMETIC\1\s*\])")


def hermetic_read():
    """The file whose code reads process.env.E2E_HERMETIC (by HERMETIC_FILES' order), or None."""
    for pattern in HERMETIC_FILES:
        for p in sorted(ROOT.glob(pattern)):
            if KNOB.search(code_text(p.read_text())):
                return p.relative_to(ROOT).as_posix()
    return None


EXPORTS_RUN = re.compile(r"\bmodule\s*\.\s*exports\s*\.\s*run\s*=[^=]")
EXPORTS_OBJ = re.compile(r"\bmodule\s*\.\s*exports\s*=\s*\{")
RUN_KEY = re.compile(r"(?:^|[{,])\s*(?:async\s+)?\*?\s*(?:run|(['\"])run\1)\s*[(:,}]|(?:^|[{,])\s*run\s*$")


def exports_run(text):
    """Whether a scenario's code exports a run, as run.js calls it: a key `run` at the
    top level of the object assigned to module.exports, or module.exports.run = .."""
    code = code_text(text)
    if EXPORTS_RUN.search(code):
        return True
    for m in EXPORTS_OBJ.finditer(code):
        depth, top, j = 1, [], m.end()
        while j < len(code) and depth:
            ch = code[j]
            if ch in "{[(":
                depth += 1
            elif ch in "}])":
                depth -= 1
            if depth == 1 or (depth == 2 and ch in "{[("):
                top.append(ch)
            elif depth == 0:
                top.append("}")
            j += 1
        if RUN_KEY.search("{" + "".join(top)):
            return True
    return False


def e2e_rows():
    if not path(SCENARIOS).is_dir():
        return [Row("e2e scenarios", ABSENT, "", f"`{SCENARIOS}/`")]
    count = len([p for p in path(SCENARIOS).iterdir()
                 if p.name.endswith(".js") and p.is_file() and exports_run(p.read_text())])
    where = hermetic_read()
    flag = Row("hermetic flag `E2E_HERMETIC`", "present" if where else "absent", "",
               f"`{where}`" if where else "`tests/e2e/run.js`, `tests/e2e/lib/`",
               {"e2e:hermetic": 1 if where else 0})
    return [Row("e2e scenarios", str(count), "", f"`{SCENARIOS}/`", {"e2e:scenarios": count}), flag]


def rows():
    return (ratchet_rows() + wire_rows() + consumer_rows() + arch_rows()
            + mutation_rows() + fuzz_rows() + bench_rows() + e2e_rows() + differential_rows())


def table(all_rows):
    out = ["| row | value | measured | record |", "|---|---:|---|---|"]
    out += ["| {} | {} | {} | {} |".format(*r.cells) for r in all_rows]
    return "\n".join(out) + "\n"


def values(all_rows):
    out = {}
    for r in all_rows:
        out.update(r.values)
    return out


def load_base(file):
    name = f"--base {file}"
    try:
        text = Path(file).read_text()
    except OSError as e:
        fail(name, "(the file)", f"not readable ({e})")
    try:
        base = json.loads(text)
    except json.JSONDecodeError as e:
        fail(name, "(the file)", f"not JSON ({e})")
    require_object(name, "(the file)", base)
    if base.get("schema") != 1:
        fail(name, "schema", "must be 1")
    vals = require_object(name, "values", base.get("values"))
    for key, v in vals.items():
        if MEASURED_KEYS.match(key):
            if not isinstance(v, bool):
                fail(name, f"values.{key}", "must be true or false")
        elif LIST_KEYS.match(key):
            if not isinstance(v, list) or not all(isinstance(e, str) and e for e in v):
                fail(name, f"values.{key}", "must be a list of names")
        elif FLOOR_KEYS.match(key) or CEILING_KEYS.match(key) or LATEST_KEYS.match(key):
            if not is_num(v):
                fail(name, f"values.{key}", "must be a number")
        else:
            fail(name, f"values.{key}", "is not a key this tool compares")
    if any(MEASURED_KEYS.match(k) for k in vals):
        for key in vals:
            if is_floor(key) and f"{key}:measured" not in vals:
                fail(name, f"values.{key}:measured", "missing; the base says whether its other floors were measured")
    return vals


def is_floor(key):
    """A mutation floor's own key, floor:<file> (not its flag, not floor:files)."""
    return key.startswith("floor:") and not MEASURED_KEYS.match(key) and not LIST_KEYS.match(key)


def ceiling(tree, scores):
    """Rules 1 and 4 of the floors' rule, on the tree alone: the faults, one per
    floor above its measured score rounded down, and the notices, one per
    provisional floor (scores: the tree's docs/scoreboard/mutants.json, by file).
    Every --check runs it, with --base or without, so the two cannot drift."""
    out, notices = [], []
    for key in sorted(k for k in tree if is_floor(k)):
        t, score = tree[key], scores.get(key[len("floor:"):])
        if score is None:
            notices.append(f"{key}: {t:g} in the tree, no measurement in the tree's record; "
                           "a provisional floor, held to no score until a night measures its file")
        elif t > math.floor(score):
            out.append(f"{key}: measured {score:g} in the tree's record, floor {t:g} in the tree; "
                       f"a floor is never above the measured score rounded down: {math.floor(score)}, not {t:g}")
    return out, notices


def falls(base, tree, scores):
    """Every value of the tree that moved the wrong way from the base's: a number
    that fell (or rose, for an allowlist), a list that lost an element, a key
    that vanished, a floor that fell against rules 2 and 3 of the floors' rule
    (scores: the tree's docs/scoreboard/mutants.json, by file); and the notices,
    one per provisional floor its first measurement lowered. A floor above its
    score is ceiling()'s, never this function's."""
    out, notices = [], []
    for key in sorted(base):
        b, t = base[key], tree.get(key)
        if t is None:
            out.append(f"a key may not vanish: {key}")
        elif MEASURED_KEYS.match(key):
            if b and not t:
                out.append(f"{key}: measured at the base, unmeasured in the tree; a measurement may not vanish")
        elif is_floor(key):
            score = scores.get(key[len("floor:"):])
            if t >= b:
                pass
            elif base.get(f"{key}:measured", False):
                out.append(f"{key}: {b:g} at the base, {t:g} in the tree; a measured floor may not fall")
            elif score is None:
                out.append(f"{key}: {b:g} at the base, {t:g} in the tree; it may not fall "
                           "(a provisional floor may not be lowered without a night's measurement)")
            elif t < math.floor(score):
                out.append(f"{key}: measured {score:g} in the tree's record, floor {t:g} in the tree; "
                           f"a provisional floor takes the measured score rounded down: {math.floor(score)}, not {t:g}")
            elif t == math.floor(score):
                notices.append(f"{key}: {b:g} at the base (provisional, unmeasured), {t:g} in the tree "
                               "(measured); the first measurement replaces a provisional floor once")
            # Above the score rounded down: the ceiling's fault (rule 1).
        elif LIST_KEYS.match(key):
            for lost in sorted(set(b) - set(t)):
                out.append(f"{key}: {lost} at the base, gone from the tree; a list may not lose an element")
        elif FLOOR_KEYS.match(key):
            if t < b:
                out.append(f"{key}: {b:g} at the base, {t:g} in the tree; it may not fall")
        elif LATEST_KEYS.match(key):
            pass  # The latest run's own figure: held only to not vanishing (above).
        elif t > b:
            why = "an allowlist may not grow" if key.startswith("allowlist:") else "it may not rise"
            out.append(f"{key}: {b:g} at the base, {t:g} in the tree; {why}")
    return out, notices


def split_doc(text):
    if text.count(BEGIN) != 1 or text.count(END) != 1 or text.index(BEGIN) > text.index(END):
        raise SystemExit(f"scoreboard: {DOC} must hold {BEGIN} once, then {END} once")
    head, rest = text.split(BEGIN)
    body, tail = rest.split(END)
    return head, body, tail


def main():
    global ROOT
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__.splitlines()[0])
    mode = ap.add_mutually_exclusive_group()
    mode.add_argument("--render", action="store_true", help="rewrite the table in docs/NORTH-STAR.md")
    mode.add_argument("--check", action="store_true", help="exit 1 when the committed table is stale")
    mode.add_argument("--json", action="store_true", help="print the tree's comparable values")
    ap.add_argument("--base", metavar="FILE", help="with --check: the base tree's --json values")
    ap.add_argument("--root", metavar="DIR", help="the tree to read (default: this checkout)")
    args = ap.parse_args()
    if args.base and not args.check:
        ap.error("--base goes with --check")
    if args.root:
        ROOT = Path(args.root).resolve()

    all_rows = rows()
    if args.json:
        print(json.dumps({"schema": 1, "values": values(all_rows)}, indent=2, sort_keys=True))
        return 0
    fresh = table(all_rows)
    if not (args.render or args.check):
        sys.stdout.write(fresh)
        return 0
    doc = path(DOC)
    head, body, tail = split_doc(doc.read_text())
    want = "\n" + fresh
    if args.render:
        if body != want:
            doc.write_text(head + BEGIN + want + END + tail)
            print(f"scoreboard: rendered {DOC}")
        else:
            print(f"scoreboard: {DOC} is current")
        return 0
    status = 0
    if body == want:
        print(f"scoreboard: {DOC} is current")
    else:
        diff = difflib.unified_diff(body.splitlines(keepends=True), want.splitlines(keepends=True),
                                    f"{DOC} (committed)", "the records (tools/scoreboard)")
        sys.stdout.writelines(diff)
        print(f"scoreboard: {DOC} is stale; run python3 tools/scoreboard --render and commit it")
        status = 1
    scores = measured_scores()[0]
    above, notices = ceiling(values(all_rows), scores)
    for line in notices:
        print(f"scoreboard: notice: {line}")
    for line in above:
        print(f"scoreboard: {line}")
    if above:
        n = len(above)
        print(f"scoreboard: {n} floor{' stands' if n == 1 else 's stand'} above "
              f"{'its measured score' if n == 1 else 'their measured scores'} rounded down")
        status = 1
    if args.base:
        base = load_base(args.base)
        fell, notices = falls(base, values(all_rows), scores)
        for line in notices:
            print(f"scoreboard: notice: {line}")
        for line in fell:
            print(f"scoreboard: {line}")
        if fell:
            print(f"scoreboard: {len(fell)} numbers moved the wrong way from the base ({args.base})")
            status = 1
        else:
            print(f"scoreboard: no number moved the wrong way from the base ({len(base)} values)")
    return status


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
